                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "stereo":</h3><p>Stereo microphones have two separate capsules mounted in close proximity to one another, and are designed to capture a stereo image of the sound source. Such mics have two separate outputs &#8212; usually <em>left</em> and <em>right</em>, but in the case of mid-side mics (in which a cardioid capsule is paired with a figure-of-8 capsule mounted 90&deg; to the cardioid) the output channels could be <em>mid</em> and <em>side</em>. Stereo mics are typically designed to eliminate phasing problems inherent in using two standalone mics to capture a stereo image.</p>
